<%#
  The sheet's own way to complain. A search that finds nothing says what the
  visitor wanted; only a print says what was wrong with it, and the visitor
  looking at the bad page is the only one who knows.

  The link carries both answers — the surface, and the answer the feedback page
  then arrives with already chosen — so this prompt asks nothing of the visitor.
  `page_key` is the sheet the visit just generated, which is also what keeps a
  page Turbo restores from reporting the showing twice.
%>
<% if local_assigns[:page_key].present? %>
  <p class="feedback-prompt no-print"
     data-analytics-page-response="Feedback Prompt Shown"
     data-analytics-response-key="<%= page_key %>">
    <%= t("shared.feedback_prompt.message") %>
    <%= link_to t("shared.feedback_prompt.action"),
          feedback_path(surface: "sheet", reason: "print_problem") %>
  </p>
<% end %>
